# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_stale_graph_failclosed.py" "STALE GRAPH FAILCLOSED GATE: PASS" "stale-graph withheld-clear (G1): a would-be clear over a behind + un-healed main graph is withheld, not falsely emitted" "stale-graph withheld-clear silent-miss (G1, a wrong-clear-on-stale-graph): when main's STORED graph is BEHIND its current HEAD (a missed/lagged push) and the pre-analysis self-heal did NOT bring it current, the brain computes the coordination view against a STALE baseline. Today ONLY the free-tier-wall sub-case is caught (_pr_quota_paused_result fires on heal reason 'free-tier limit'); EVERY OTHER heal failure [a transient GitHub read error, a network/timeout, a permission blip, a re-ingest failure] falls through, so a would-be 'clear' is emitted against the stale graph -> a real overlap whose graph edge only exists at the newer HEAD is MISSED -> a SILENT false clear. THE FIX [recall-safe]: when the stored graph was BEHIND HEAD and self-heal did NOT produce a current graph [for ANY reason other than the quota wall, which keeps its own more specific note], a would-be 'clear' [check conclusion 'success'] is WITHHELD and replaced by an advisory 'neutral' 'code graph not confirmed current -- not cleared' check + comment [content-free, jargon-free, idempotent in-place upsert, never-crash]. It ONLY downgrades a would-be CLEAR -- a heads-up / wait-in-line [material 'neutral'] verdict on the SAME stale graph is still shown [over-flagging is safe; the bug is under-flagging]. The behind-and-not-current signal is derived from the self_heal_main_graph return WITHOUT a second HEAD read [head_sha present AND not healed AND reason != 'already current']; 'behind is None' [HEAD unresolvable] and 'behind is False' [already current / healed to current] are NEVER downgraded. Drives the REAL handler [server.handle_event] over the REAL gate [db/schema.sql] with a FakeGitHub whose self-heal re-ingest RAISES while main HEAD is ahead of the stored graph" "stale-graph withheld-clear [G1]: a would-be clear over a BEHIND + un-healed main graph is withheld as an advisory 'not confirmed current' [neutral], while a real collision on the same behind graph still surfaces [action_required], a heal that SUCCEEDED keeps its clear [success], and an unresolvable HEAD [behind None] is now withheld to the separate G1-tail 'currency not confirmed' advisory [neutral] while _graph_degraded stays False for it [behind-and-not-current path unchanged] -- recall-safe" 20
